<title>UK: CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-ENGLISH COUNTY CHAMPIONSHIP SCORES.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Close of play scores on the</p>
<p>second day of four-day English County Championship cricket</p>
<p>matches on Thursday:</p>
<p>At Cheltenham: Derbyshire 120 and 174-3 (K.Barnett 51 not</p>
<p>out).</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 484 (S.Young 237, M.Alleyne 97, T.Hancock 54;</p>
<p>D.Malcolm 4-102).</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Kent 498-9 (M.Ealham 139, S.Marsh 98 not out,</p>
<p>P.Strang 82, T.Ward 51; J.Ormond 5-107) v Leicestershire.</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Lancashire 561-8 declared (N.Fairbrother</p>
<p>132, J.Crawley 112, I.Austin 78 not out, M.Watkinson 75). Sussex</p>
<p>156-5 (N.Taylor 82).</p>
<p>At Northampton: Northamptonshire 364 (D.Roberts 117;</p>
<p>P.Grayson 4-53) and 14-0. Essex 275 (N.Hussain 77, P.Prichard</p>
<p>50; K.Curran 4-32).</p>
<p>At Trent Bridge: Warwickshire 344 (D.Hemp 70, D.Ostler 65;</p>
<p>C.Tolley 4-92, P.Franks 4-81). Nottinghamshire 93-7 (D.Brown</p>
<p>4-29).</p>
<p>At Guildford: Surrey 477 (A.Stewart 98, G.Thorpe 84, C.Lewis</p>
<p>76, A.Hollioake 75, M.Butcher 69). Hampshire 200-5 (M.Hayden</p>
<p>58).</p>
<p>At Scarborough: Durham 152 and 61-5. Yorkshire 372</p>
<p>(D.Lehmann 86, B.Parker 74 not out, A.McGrath 57).</p>
</text>
